WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.003 --> 00:00:04.170
FERNANDA DE LA TORRE: The
brain's ability to imagine

00:00:04.170 --> 00:00:05.970
is a fascinating mystery.

00:00:05.970 --> 00:00:08.940
I grew up in Mexico, and my
small family crossed the border

00:00:08.940 --> 00:00:12.570
because we imagined a better
life in the United States.

00:00:12.570 --> 00:00:15.780
Later, I escaped an abusive
home because I imagined a better

00:00:15.780 --> 00:00:17.250
future for myself.

00:00:17.250 --> 00:00:19.710
And much later, my
imagination inspired

00:00:19.710 --> 00:00:21.960
me to dream of having a
job where I could ponder

00:00:21.960 --> 00:00:23.820
the largest questions of life.

00:00:23.820 --> 00:00:26.670
I'm Fernanda De La Torre, and
at the McGovern Institute,

00:00:26.670 --> 00:00:28.950
I use math to study how
our brain understands

00:00:28.950 --> 00:00:32.070
the difference between
imagination and reality.

00:00:32.070 --> 00:00:33.600
Let me give you an example.

00:00:33.600 --> 00:00:35.730
Follow the motion
of this pink cube.

00:00:35.730 --> 00:00:37.980
Do you imagine it dropping
onto the purple surface

00:00:37.980 --> 00:00:40.010
or sliding down a ramp?

00:00:40.010 --> 00:00:41.600
It's hard to tell, right?

00:00:41.600 --> 00:00:43.490
That's because the
visual clues are vague,

00:00:43.490 --> 00:00:44.865
and the movement
of the pink cube

00:00:44.865 --> 00:00:47.540
could be caused by different
physical realities.

00:00:47.540 --> 00:00:50.675
Now, what if I pair the same
video with a sound clue?

00:00:50.675 --> 00:00:54.860
[SCRAPING SOUND]

00:00:54.860 --> 00:00:55.880
Now it's obvious.

00:00:55.880 --> 00:00:58.313
The cube is clearly
sliding down the ramp.

00:00:58.313 --> 00:00:59.730
That's because
your brain combined

00:00:59.730 --> 00:01:01.670
the visual clues
and the sound clues

00:01:01.670 --> 00:01:04.489
to determine what was really
happening with the cube.

00:01:04.489 --> 00:01:06.300
I use artificial
neural networks,

00:01:06.300 --> 00:01:08.990
or a series of math
equations, to understand

00:01:08.990 --> 00:01:11.600
how the brain makes these
important mental calculations

00:01:11.600 --> 00:01:15.280
so that we can distinguish
imagination from reality.

